  "strategy": "Approach and rationale:\nWe aim to improve the upper bound for the Erd\u0151s minimum overlap problem by minimizing the maximum overlap integral C5. The core idea is to modify and optimize a binary step function from the initial parent structure. We focus on three key areas to reduce C5:\n1. Improve load distribution by reducing peaks in the autocorrelation function\n2. Create more temporal separation between active intervals by adjusting placements\n3. Mitigate boundary effects through strategic cross-overs\n\nOur approach avoids direct solver usage due to non-convexity and provides an efficient restart mechanism for local optimization. We balance depth and width of searches to explore promising variations without excessive computation.\n\nMathematicalspecification:\n- Representation: h[i] \u2208 [0,1] for i=0 to n_points-1, sum(h) = n_points/2 exactly\n- Objective: min C5 = max_k dx * |np.correlate(h, 1-h, mode='full')[k]| \n- Constraints: 0 \u2264 h[i] \u2264 1 for all i, sum(h) = n_points/2\n- Initialization: Start with initial_h_values and target low-C structure\n- Repair method: Project to feasible set via clipping and sum-normalization\n\nImplementationprocedure:\n1. Validation: Verify initial_h_values satisfies all constraints\n2. Optimization initialization: Use target_h_proj as starting point\n3. Multi-stage update:\n   Stage 0: Global search with broad perturbations\n   Stage 1: Local refinement with window-based operations\n   Stage 2: Intensification focusing near current best regions\n4. Candidate repair: Adjust sum via stochastic balancing\n5. Feasibility check: Verify against constraints after each update\n6. Score evaluation: Compute C5 using full correlation\n\nFor solver-free optimization:\n- Create search space of variations above 0.3700\n- For distances > 0.3750, perform grid-based localization\n- Randomized sampling follows hierarchical structure\n\nSearchchoicesandusefulvariations:\n- Default configuration:\n  - Initial_window = 0.380876\n  - Perturbation_size = 0.02\n  - Step_window = 0.015\n  - Max_iter = 300\n- Triggered variations:\n  - Population diversity reduction when stuck\n  - Cross-over with parent solution when necessary\n  - Adaptive windowing based on improvement rate\n\nComputebudgetandrobustness:\n- Time estimates:\n  - Initial: 10 seconds\n  - Local search: 800 seconds\n  - Intensification: 200 seconds\n- Schedule: Prioritize improvement before timeout\n- Main loop size: 500 points typically sufficient\n  Fallback: Return parent solution if no improvement\n- Validity: Maintain binary structure and exact length\n\nValidationandreturncontract:\n- Feasibility checks:\n  \u2022 0 \u2264 h[i] \u2264 1 for all i\n  \u2022 sum(h) = n_points/2 exactly\n- Score computation:\n  - Exact correlation with original implementation\n  - No gradient/Lagrange methods for correctness\n- Output format: 3-distinct array, computed score\n- Stability: Fallback registered before execution\n\nWe independently validate each candidate with direct correlation metric to ensure objective accuracy. Returns only non-dominated solutions meeting C < 0.3809.",
